 ## Current reviewer considerations
 
 Source SHA-256: `f7b18a5c8e7347d5555c1cea11c2a2d5375817be63a7c6ae1489601c98456868`.
+
+### Open bounded finding: the three-corner condition survives teaching
+
+The source above always constructs four-cell targets with at least three literal
+bbox corners. A protected-Racket rival that requires both exactly four cells and
+at least three bbox corners fits all three direct-generated demonstrations at
+seed `424203`, medium difficulty, indices `0..2`. Both programs also agree on the
+preserved production-sampled query at index `3`. Moving that query's non-corner
+target within its unchanged bbox to retain only two corners creates a lawful
+stress query accepted by both `self_check` and `lesson_identifiable`; the canonical
+program fills the target and the rival erases it. This query was constructed,
+not production-sampled. The original lesson and alternative-answer candidate are
+retained separately; no native lesson export or production-query failure is claimed.
+
+Reproducer: `workspace/probe_three_corners.py`, requiring a fresh `--out` path.
+Source-bound retained evidence: `counterexamples/three-corners/`; original command
+and evidence: `checks/42fb6b33deea/three-corners-command.json` and
+`checks/42fb6b33deea/three-corners/` in the review workspace. Public files contain
+only demonstration pairs and one query input; programs and query answers are
+private. Ten protected-Racket applications passed, with all six demonstration
+applications completed before query execution. Proposed repair: schedule an
+exact-four witness with at most two bbox corners and declare this geometry-plus-
+count rival, or explicitly narrow the lawful grammar. No production repair was
+made. **Owner acceptance: pending/not performed. Training admitted: false.**
 
