 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Open bounded peer finding: capped-count lesson ambiguity
+
+`counterexamples/cap-ambiguity/` retains a protected-Racket replay on selected
+generator SHA-256 `1bb0029217dfe3bc4d19aeed64933a5d41db97231c4596a74253544ff650e5b9`.
+Three direct `generate(seed=1, sample_index=0..2)` demonstrations have top/bottom
+counts `(3,1)`, `(1,0)`, `(1,2)`. The canonical cap-four program and a cap-three
+rival both fit all three, then disagree on direct production draw index 3
+(`top_cap`, counts `(5,2)`), which passes `self_check`. Both programs execute in
+the live protected Racket backend; exceptions fail the probe. This is one
+chosen direct-sampler lesson, not a native lesson export or a universal failure.
+
+The reusable probe is `workspace/cap_ambiguity_probe.py`; its `--out` refuses an
+existing file, directory, or symlink. The retained report binds runtime identity,
+program/probe/source hashes and the public-byte challenge ID. Only `public.json`
+contains the model-visible challenge (three labeled demos and one query input);
+programs, query labels, the original lesson and alternative-answer candidate
+are retained separately under `private/`. The exact command receipt and output
+refusal checks are included. Originals remain at
+`checks/e971e0773705/cap-ambiguity/` and
+`checks/e971e0773705/cap-ambiguity-command.json` in this review workspace.
+
+Proposed repair for lesson construction: include a count-four-or-higher
+demonstration before a capped-count query, or check identification against this
+cap-three rival. Production source was not modified. Owner acceptance is
+**pending/not performed**; `training_admitted=false`.
